# Think Live Monitor Best Practices

Source mirror: `.agent-sources/cloudflare-agents` at commit `8ad724b` from `https://github.com/cloudflare/agents`.

Files read:

- `.agent-sources/cloudflare-agents/docs/think/index.md`
- `.agent-sources/cloudflare-agents/docs/think/sub-agents.md`
- `.agent-sources/cloudflare-agents/docs/think/programmatic-submissions.md`
- `.agent-sources/cloudflare-agents/docs/think/lifecycle-hooks.md`
- `.agent-sources/cloudflare-agents/docs/think/tools.md`

## Findings for Agent Dungeon

- Use `subAgent(...).chat()` when the parent Referee needs live stream forwarding from child Think agents. It exposes `onStart`, `onEvent`, `onDone`, and `onError`, which fits the live monitor better than waiting on `saveMessages()`.
- Use `submitMessages()` when a caller needs fast durable acceptance, idempotency, and later status inspection. This fits operator-triggered work where request timeouts would make retry state ambiguous.
- Use `startFiber()` for the app-owned run supervisor around the turns, not as a replacement for Think's own durable turn ledger.
- Use `beforeTurn()` to control the tavern-turn shape: active tools, max steps, `sendReasoning`, timeouts, and model override.
- Use custom tools for intentional process reporting (`report_player_process`, `report_referee_process`), but do not force the final submit tool too early or the model cannot report WIP.
- Use `onChunk()` and `sendReasoning: true` for live monitor streams when provider/model emits chunks.
- For browser/live monitor UX, persist process events in Referee state and replay them on reconnect. Socket-only events are not enough.

## Current mismatch to fix next

The prototype still mixes `saveMessages()` and global event forwarding for retained child agents. Better shape:

1. Referee run supervisor owns the beat fiber.
2. Parent calls each child via `child.chat(prompt, callback)` for player and Referee Think turns.
3. Callback `onEvent(json)` forwards real child chunks to the Referee monitor socket and persists compact process events.
4. Use `onStart` request ids for cancellation and pause/reset.
5. Keep direct structured model calls as fallback only when Think/tool streaming fails.

## Package compatibility note

Tried updating `@cloudflare/think` from `^0.7.2` to `0.7.3` after checking upstream package version, but reverted because `@cloudflare/think@0.7.3` imports newer `agents/chat` exports (`createChatFiberSnapshot`, `unwrapChatFiberSnapshot`, `wrapChatFiberSnapshot`) that are not exported by the currently installed `agents@0.13.2`.

Keep `@cloudflare/think` on `0.7.2` unless `agents` is upgraded to a compatible version too.
